<Base title="Affiliate Disclosure" path="/affiliate-disclosure/" description="How TechMintAI may use affiliate links, advertising and sponsored content to support the website.">
<div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Affiliate Disclosure</div><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">How we earn</span><h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1><p>Free content still takes work. Here is how TechMintAI may earn revenue.</p></header><div class="legal"><h2>Affiliate relationships</h2><p>Some links on TechMintAI may become affiliate links. When a reader follows an affiliate link and makes a qualifying purchase or sign-up, TechMintAI may receive a commission at no additional charge to the reader, depending on the program. An affiliate disclosure will appear near content containing such links.</p><h2>Advertising</h2><p>We may also earn revenue from display advertising. Ads will be distinguishable from articles or guides. Showing an advertisement is not an endorsement of the advertiser.</p><h2>Sponsored content</h2><p>If TechMintAI publishes paid placements, we intend to identify them clearly as “Sponsored” or “Advertisement” and distinguish them from independent editorial articles.</p><h2>Our editorial standards</h2><p>Our aim is to recommend evaluation criteria that readers can verify for themselves. We should not describe a product as independently tested unless it has actually been tested. See <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p><p>At launch, no affiliate partnership or income is implied by the existence of this page. Actual affiliate links must be disclosed individually when added.</p></div></div>
</Base>
